## Why Juniper Health exists

Living with a long-term health condition is hard enough. Trying to understand it, and then working out what help you can get, can feel overwhelming. Official information is often long, complicated and full of jargon.

Juniper Health is here to make it simpler. We:

- **explain health conditions** in plain English, based on NHS and NICE information
- **explain disability benefits** such as PIP, Attendance Allowance and DLA, step by step
- **build free self-checks** that help you see which parts of a benefit may apply to you
- **point you to trusted help,** such as the NHS, charities and free advice services

## Our promises

- **Free to use.** Our guides and self-checks will always be free.
- **Plain English.** We write so anyone can understand, without jargon.
- **Private by design.** Our self-checks run on your own device. We never see your answers.
- **Honest.** We tell you what the rules really say, including when a claim may be hard.
- **Independent.** We are not part of the DWP, the NHS or any company that sells benefit services.

## Who we are

Juniper Health was set up by [Neil Hyde](/about/neil-hyde/), who writes and edits the guides. It is run as a small independent business.

## How we check our facts

Every page is based on official and trusted sources, such as GOV.UK, the law on legislation.gov.uk, the NHS and NICE. We list our sources on each page and check every page at least once a year. Read our [editorial policy](/about/editorial-policy/).

## How we are funded

We are funded by donations and by a small number of clearly labelled affiliate links. We do not show adverts. Read [how we make money](/affiliate-disclosure/).

## What we are building next

We started with **fibromyalgia** and the three main disability benefits. We are adding more health conditions over time. If there is a condition you would like us to cover, [let us know](/contact/).
